NeoForge 1.21.10 port (zakoopt/neoforge-1.21.10) — what was changed:
- the layered sources of the Fabric 1.21.10 module (common, 1.21.x, 1.21.4-1.21.10, 1.21.8+, 1.21.9+,
  1.21.8-1.21.11, 1.21.8-1.21.10, 1.21.9-1.21.11, 1.21.10) are copied into one NeoForge project (ModDevGradle);
- FabricLoader calls are replaced by zako.opt.Platform (NeoForge's loading mod list, config dir, dev check);
- zako.opt.Mods looks mods up in NeoForge's mod list;
- MovingBlockCache renders through NeoForge's RenderTypeHelper.getMovingBlockRenderType instead of the
  Fabric Renderer API's RenderLayerHelper.movingDelegate;
- the Mod Menu entry is replaced by NeoForge's IConfigScreenFactory (zako.opt.ZakoOptMod);
- fabric.mod.json is replaced by META-INF/neoforge.mods.toml;
- mixins into BlockEntityRenderDispatcher.tryExtractRenderState name the overload NeoForge adds (with Frustum);
- GuiRendererMixin and LevelRendererOutlineMixin target the lambdas by their NeoForge names
  (lambda$prepareItemElements$3, lambda$addMainPass$1) instead of Fabric's intermediary method_71055 / method_62214;
- BatchableBufferSourceMixin no longer lists the intermediary name of getBuffer.
